DICTIONARIES: dictionary is used to data in key:value pair
  ex: 
student={"name":"bob"},{"cgpa":7}
print(student)

  dDICTIONARIES METHODS : 
suppose 

  student={"name":"bob"},{"age":20},{"city":"blr"}

1.KEYS(): keys are returns all keys values(lest side values)

2.VALUES() : values are all right side items 

3.ITEM() : it returns all key values pairs
  ex: 
student={"name":"bob"},{"age":20},{"city":"blr"}
print(student)

4.GET(KEY): IT RETURNS THE VALUE OD THE KEY
  EX: 
student = {"name": "bob", "age": 20, "city": "blr"}
print(student.get("name"))

5.UPDATE(): used to change the values 
  ex: 
student = {"name": "bob", "age": 20, "city": "blr"}
student.update({"city":"mysore"})
print(student)
